From 3c9bc78cd2f8d2c9e35ed83cb9573c15144af16a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:53:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/45] Send entity variables, corpses and rubble in the
 Specula feed

Feed format v14. CCmpVisualActor::SetVariable only hands a variable to
the model, which a nonvisual engine has none of, so it now also keeps
it, and ICmpVisual::GetVariables returns them. The turn record's entity
gains a variable set index after its variant set, and the new kind 16
variable set record lists the names and values, so the web view's
particles read numbuilders as the construction dust does.

Besides the construction previews, the local entities whose template is
"corpse|" or "decay|" (the rubble of SpawnEntityOnDeath) are now sent:
they carry the destruction smoke and dust. Mirages and placement
previews stay out.
